  "problema": "OeisA357513.general_supercongruence",
  "oeis": "A357513",
  "righe": [
   "%C A357513 This conjecture is now proved; see Links. The exceptional primes are exactly the primes p for which p - 1 divides 2*m + 4 and p does not divide 2*m + 7. In particular, p = 2 is always exceptional, and for m = 1 the exceptions are p = 2 and p = 7 (only p = 7 when restricted to p >= 3). Every exceptional prime satisfies p <= 2*m + 5. - _Ondrej Kutal_, Jul 18 2026",
   "%H A357513 Moritz Firsching, <a href=\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/879bf00811ed2e504511fe6f78b59605fddcfa31/FormalConjectures/OEIS/357513.lean\">AlphaProof proof of a conjecture</a>, Jan 2026.",
   "%H A357513 Ondrej Kutal, <a href=\"https://github.com/TheSil/A357513_conjecture\">A proof of the generalized conjecture, with Lean formalization</a>, Jul 2026."
  ]
